
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use any algorithm, implementation, methodology, or
  experimental result from this repository, please cite this
  software. Please also consult the relevant algorithm-specific
  Markdown documentation for additional academic attribution
  and references, including PhD thesis attribution where applicable.

type: software

title: "A Collection of Reinforcement Learning Algorithms"

authors:
  - family-names: "Stafford"
    given-names: "Ronnie"

version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-02"

url: "https://github.com/ronniestafford/ai-ml-research"

license: MIT

abstract: >-
  An open-source collection of reinforcement learning algorithms,
  implementations, and experimental tools. The repository includes
  multiple reinforcement learning methods, covering model-based,
  value-based, and deep reinforcement learning. It supports
  research, experimentation, benchmarking, and reproducibility.
  Individual algorithms may originate from the author's PhD research
  or other published academic work. Users should consult the
  corresponding Markdown documentation and citation.bib for algorithm-specific
  provenance and citation requirements.

keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - model-based reinforcement learning
  - value-based reinforcement learning
  - deep reinforcement learning
  - reinforcement learning algorithms
  - artificial intelligence
  - machine learning
  - open-source software
  - academic research

